08:39:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T00:02:17Z","closed_at":"2026-01-26T19:19:59Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115089","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115089","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115089.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115089.patch","merged_at":"2026-01-26T19:19:59Z"},"body":"Fixed an issue where collide/cast shape against a triangle would return a hit result with mShape2Face in incorrect winding order. This caused an incorrect normal in the enhanced internal edge removal algorithm. This in turn resulted in objects not settling properly on dense triangle grids.\r\n\r\nIn godot, the height field data is provided in a mirrored way compared to Jolt. To compensate for this, Jolt's height field shapes are always scaled by (1 1 -1) in `JoltHeightMapShape3D::_build_height_field`. This is why we were hitting this particular edge case.\r\n\r\nFixes #115009","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":